WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
This is the story of a dragon

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.780
with poison in his heart

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.860
And it's the story of the race that discovered him

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:10.120
worshipped his Magnificence but ultimately perished by his side.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.880
Dragons have always been intriguing to humanity, with many believing they hold the secrets to life itself.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.940
One who believed this was Vendrick, king of Drangleic and his brother Aldia.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:28.080
Together they experimented on dragons in the hopes that they could learn more about their existence.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.660
Eventually, they were successful, recreating an ancient dragon with the ability to peer into the past

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.960
to view the stories of old so that they might learn from them.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.840
This is one such story.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.160
In the Ancient Dragon's Eerie, before the chamber with the dragons egg

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:51.840
is a mural that depicts and ancient civilisation who existed long ago, deep below the deepest depths.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.040
Legend has it that deep below the earth behind a door locked from the inside is a magnificent city built for a

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.640
built for a great slumbering dragon.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.540
In a bygone age the king in the depths built his city around this beast

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.840
this subterranean world centered around the great sanctum that housed the dragon in its depths

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.140
and was aptly named Shulva, the Sanctum city.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.940
This was a religious city where sorceries were considered taboo but miracles flourished

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.860
as the people there were grounded in their faith.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.200
The people prayed and worshipped and the priestesses sang to soothe the dragon in its slumber.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.320
One wonders whether a single phrase of their song ever reached the dragon's ears

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.460
but to people of faith such questions matter not.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:44.940
As is common "the King had a dear Queen" and the Queen sang to the dragon also.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.400
At this point in our story you should know that the dragon has a tragic  secret

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:57.340
deep within him, Sinh harbours a dreadful store of poison and there will come a time where he cannot bear

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.160
any longer.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.180
Looking back it's impossible to know whether the people knew of the poison

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.320
or even if the dragon himself knew.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.420
Perhaps the people of the city prayed, sang and soothed out of fear

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.020
fear that the waking of the dragon would lead to their demise

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.080
if so, this could only serve to strengthen thier faith

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.740
for fear is the heart of reverence and the people revered their magnificent sleeping beast

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.180
the centre of their faith.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.840
It should come as no surprise to you that men would come to covet the dragon.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.760
To the Drakeblood Knights fresh dragon blood was sacrosanct.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.000
They believed that by obtaining it they could come to a true understanding of life

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.320
allowing them to transcend their own pointless existence.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.760
In a world where strength of purpose keeps one from hollowing a belief like this isn't so strange.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.440
Lead by sir Yorgh and his famous spear, the drakeblood knights lay siege to Shulva.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.920
The king of Shulva called his Sanctum knights to arm

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.380
many of whom renounced their own flesh to eternally guard the sanctum from the assault of Sir Yhorg

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.520
and his Drakeblood Knights.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.000
They were sentenced to eternal stewardship yet soon the day would come

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.700
where the sanctum received nary a visitor.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.040
During the conflict the dragon slept lulled by the queen's song.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.780
You have to wonder who sent Sir Yhorg and his Drakeblood Knights

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.660
so look now upon the crest of Sir Yhorg and see the truth of things.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.860
This is the crest of Drangleic.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.700
Sir Yhorg, leader of the Drakeblood Knights and possibly of Vendrick's kingdom.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.480
Cuts down the soldiers of the sanctum and kills the king in the depths

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.540
he then faces the Slumbering Dragon

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.880
With visions of Dragon Blood and Omniscience, Sir Yhorg pierces the Dragon with a flash of his steel

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.680
piercing Sinh through the chest

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.480
and as you can imagine it wasn't what he was expecting.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.420
Sinh immediately awakens and from his wounds spews forth the deadly poison

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.080
that had long been brewing within him.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:56.200
It blankets the entire city in a miasmic cloud, restoring the Dragon's purity but toppling the city

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.940
Sir Yhorg and his Drakeblood Knights disappeared into the sanctum

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.440
And nothing more was heard of the race that discovered a dragon

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.540
and worshipped its magnificence.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.220
Until now.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.380
There have been many kings and kingdoms

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:14.880
Hierarchies that rose and fell, leaving ruined kingdoms behind

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.340
We visit the memories of Vendrick, king of his own unraveled kingdom

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.280
"I am no king"

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.240
"I am more fit to be a jester..."

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.540
"I was unaware of my own blindness"

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.540
"We are feeble vessels, with feebler souls"

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.720
"we would cast aside the prop of life''

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.260
"only to face greater hardship"

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.040
"are you another such fool?"

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.320
"or something more?"

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.760
"seeker of fire, conqueror of dark"

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.420
"Do you intend to link the fire?"

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.420
"then you must first take the throne."

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.100
"Prove your worth"

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.420
"Find the ancient crowns"

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.740
"Seek adversity and they will be yours"

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.580
"and your wishes"

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.280
"Granted."

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.200
Somewhere within the sanctum is the crown of the sunken king.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.680
The crown of a king who came before Vendrick.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.640
The crown of a king who is killed by Sir Yhorg on the day that the dragon awoke

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.000
We explore the ruined sanctum and we uncover the truths that it holds.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:24.680
The soldiers in the sanctum are now undead, coated with the corrosive poison of the dragon

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.680
but still carrying out their orders to defend the Sanctum from outsiders.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.000
Throughout the Sanctum we find open chests which are a tribute to the grave robbers and thieves

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.500
who have flocked to this place.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.740
Sinh the Sleeping Dragon now roams his domain, sleeping lightly where he pleases.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.200
He even clears a bridge for us at one point, killing the two soldiers that block our path

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.940
Dragons, in all the lore, have always kept to themselves.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.980
They either think themselves above man or do not care for his conflicts.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.700
You have to wonder about Sinh, did he harbour malicious intent?

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:02.500
He had poison in his heart but when he was pierced by Yhorgs spear, the poison gushed out and restored

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.360
his purity.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:09.040
This implies he was pure before, which suggests that the poison was placed within him,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:10.720
But by whom?

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.780
We find an answer in the sanctum

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:13.740
right before Sinh.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.840
*Eerie singing*

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:17.620
"You"

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.940
"forever, you shall Rot"

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.060
Elana, the Squalid Queen

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.920
Once again sings to Sinh the Slumbering Dragon

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.840
After the kingdom is ruined by Sinh's awakening she remains, alone.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:38.700
I believe Elana sang the song of poison into the Dragon's heart

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.480
and was at least partly responsible for the fall of the Sunken King.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.460
Just like her sister Nashandra was responsible for the fall of Drangleic.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.600
Nothing explicitly confirms Elana's intentions

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.940
except the pattern that repeats itself.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:56.900
We are discovering that all great kings have queens that lay in wait

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.860
waiting for the right moment to strike

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:04.140
and it's easy to believe that the queen of the sanctum city was partly responsible for its fall.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:11.160
Elana defends her sunken kingdom with a mixture of fire, dark and, most notably, poison and filth

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:17.500
her essence is that of filth and neglect she even summons a depraved replica of the king's hand,

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.160
Velstadt

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.940
completing the image of a queen devoted to making a mire of the world.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:26.260
After we conquer Elana, we learn who she was from her soul

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.820
"Seeker of fire"

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:33.120
"I see you've subdued another foul creature"

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.960
"One of the father of the Abyss' Spawn"

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.520
"That... confounded quintessence of humanity"

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.880
"The Abyss once had form"

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.860
"But then Dissipated"

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.080
"and yet"

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.360
"traces of its existence endured"

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.080
"Each fragment thirsting for power spread dark with no relent"

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:56.080
"My dear Shandra was one such fragment"

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.660
"A feeble, tiny thing that thirsted for power more than any other"

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:06.000
"Driven by insatiable lust... for a worhty vessel."

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.660
All queens thus far are the children of the sentient Abyss that existed long ago.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:16.240
They are the pieces that regained form in ways that hinted humanities true nature.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.840
They seek to be whole once again.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:23.000
Elana, the queen of the Sanctum King, is a child of Wrath

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.540
She is gathering souls and power from the Slumbering Dragon

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.000
in anticipation of the coming day of vengence.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.860
Her sister, Nashandra, the queen of Drangleic is a child of Want

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.880
The kings dear Shandra seeks the throne and the power to reshape the world that comes with it

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.860
for this she needs a vessel.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.660
Nashandra guards the Throne, Elana guards a crown.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:49.840
I'm sure a third sister lies in the remains of the Old Iron King's kingdom

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.400
and we've yet to see her.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:55.100
It appears that the sisters are keeping the crowns and the throne warm.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.520
Waiting for some day of reckoning where they avenge their father.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:02.860
Every king of light has had a fragment of Manus undoing their efforts from the start.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.340
Like Vendrick says the 'brighter the flame the deeper their shadow'.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.060
Sinh's death was a result of our desire for the Crown of The Sunken King

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.100
for it is now our job to gather the crowns and link the fire.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.780
We aim to be a Lord of Light that the previous kings won't

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.760
and we will succeed in this.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.800
But what if... we have a queen of our own?

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.520
Emerald Herald:

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:31.360
"Bearer of the Curse, I will always be at your side"

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.960
"Until hope has fully withered."

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:49.320
End

